e that's definitely a  concern of mine and also I don't know if  this is you know directly about the  virus but you wonder okay are you going  to be able to see people you know I  think about the guys they have families  like oh are you gonna be able to see  your wife your children you know if I'm  in this bubble what am I gonna be doing  will I get to see my family that's  that's definitely a concern but I  understand that in essence for the  bubble to be a bubble you have to stay  in there and people can't go in and out  but that's something that is it's  definitely a bit of a concern of mine  and what ways can you really you know  police this area because at the end of  the day people are going to be people  we're all human I'm so intrigued by all  of this I am really looking forward to  not just the return to action but how  all of these things will be implemented  we'll all be watching it very closely  but Taylor while I have you here you  know I have to brag about your new show  you have a new long-form show coming up  on bleacher report your series will  start this Friday please tell us all  about it I'm very excited oh thank you  so much I'm really excited for it too as  you said it starts on Friday  DeMar DeRozan is guest number one and  when I was looking at you know  everything happening with this super  important movement the black lives  matter movement the social justice  movement a lot of the talk was about  where we are right now and I felt like  something that was missing was how we  got here and the emotions that many  people feel right now what has happened  in their life that has led them to feel  so strongly about the injustice is that  we see right now so the series centers  around two questions which is the first  question when did you realize that being  black meant something different from  being white and the last question is how  do you define America and through  stories and anecdotes  they are discussing how their life  affects how they 